---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
import ContactBand from '../components/ContactBand.astro';
import WorkExplorer from '../components/WorkExplorer.astro';
import StoryScene from '../components/StoryScene.astro';
import '../styles/home.css';
import {projects} from '../data/projects';
const pick=(ids:string[])=>ids.map(id=>projects.find(p=>p.id===id)!);
const built=pick(['orias','gawangdiwa','zenith']), steps=pick(['balzy','artin','komforten']), wired=pick(['vendrato']);
---
<Site title="Websites, and what happens after the click" description="Marv Pacinabao is a consultant at Vendrato. He builds websites and storefronts and connects them to the CRM, booking, automations and tracking behind them.">
<section class="st-story" id="st-story">
<StoryScene/>
<div class="st-beats">
<div class="st-beat"><div class="wrap"><div class="st-in"><h1>Websites, and what happens after the click.</h1><p class="st-lede">I’m Marv, a consultant at Vendrato. I build websites and storefronts, then connect them to the CRM, booking, automations and tracking that turn a visit into a customer.</p><div class="st-cta"><a class="button button-blue" href="https://vendrato.com/book">Book a free call</a><a class="button st-ghost" href="#selected-work">See the work</a></div></div></div></div>
<div class="st-beat" id="story"><div class="wrap"><div class="st-in"><h2>I learned to check things twice.</h2><p>My first trade was aircraft maintenance and inspection. You follow the checklist, you troubleshoot in order, and you never sign off on something you didn’t look at. I left the trade. The habit came with me.</p><a class="text-link" href="/aviation/">My aviation background</a></div></div></div>
<div class="st-beat"><div class="wrap"><div class="st-in"><h2>Then I wanted to make the thing myself.</h2><p>After a stretch doing outreach and partnerships at a startup, I learned HTML, CSS and JavaScript by hand. Page builders came later. When Elementor or a Shopify section misbehaves now, I know where to look.</p><ul class="st-proof" aria-label="Projects built this way">{built.map(p=><li><a href={`/work/${p.id}/`}><img src={`/images/shots/${p.id}.webp`} width="1440" height="1000" loading="lazy" alt=""/><span><b>{p.name}</b>{p.kind}</span></a></li>)}</ul></div></div></div>
<div class="st-beat"><div class="wrap"><div class="st-in"><h2>A page is one step, not the whole trip.</h2><p>Supporting a Sweden-based brand, I built Shopify pages, kept Funnelish funnels updated, handled translations and ran QA before campaigns. A page sits between an ad and a checkout. I build it knowing both sides.</p><ul class="st-proof" aria-label="Projects along the funnel">{steps.map(p=><li><a href={`/work/${p.id}/`}><img src={`/images/shots/${p.id}.webp`} width="1440" height="1000" loading="lazy" alt=""/><span><b>{p.name}</b>{p.kind}</span></a></li>)}</ul></div></div></div>
<div class="st-beat"><div class="wrap"><div class="st-in"><h2>Then it has to connect to something.</h2><p>That is the idea behind <a class="st-inline" href="https://vendrato.com/">Vendrato</a>, Gabriel Fordan’s web, automation and AI studio, where I’m a consultant. He works out the system. I build the pages people land on, then the part nobody sees: GoHighLevel pipelines and workflows, booking and reminders, Make and n8n automations, and the tracking that shows which ad paid for itself.</p><ul class="st-proof" aria-label="Connected project">{wired.map(p=><li><a href={`/work/${p.id}/`}><img src={`/images/shots/${p.id}.webp`} width="1440" height="1000" loading="lazy" alt=""/><span><b>{p.name}</b>{p.kind}</span></a></li>)}</ul></div></div></div>
<div class="st-beat"><div class="wrap"><div class="st-in"><h2>So I’m more than the person who builds the page.</h2><p>At Vendrato I work across the website, the CRM behind it and the automations between them. When you book a call with the studio, I’m one of the people you’ll talk to.</p><div class="st-cta"><a class="button st-ghost" href="#what-i-do">See what I do there</a></div></div></div></div>
</div>
</section>
<div class="wrap home-reel" id="selected-work"><WorkExplorer/><div class="work-archive-link"><p>Eight builds. Different brands. My attention to the details.</p><a class="text-link" href="/work/">Explore all projects</a></div></div>
<section class="st-offers" id="what-i-do"><div class="wrap">
<div class="st-head"><h2>What I do at Vendrato.</h2><p>Vendrato designs your digital presence, then builds what happens next. I work on both halves.</p></div>
<div class="st-ways">
<article><h3>Websites</h3><p class="st-price">From US$2,000</p><p>The studio handles strategy, content, design and development. My part is the build: Shopify storefronts, WordPress and Elementor sites, landing pages and advertorials, checked on every screen before launch.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://vendrato.com/websites">Vendrato websites</a></article>
<article><h3>CRM systems</h3><p class="st-price">Priced to scope</p><p>Sales process, setup, migration and team training. My part is the front of it: GoHighLevel funnels, forms, booking and lead capture, connected so a new enquiry lands in the pipeline.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://vendrato.com/crm">Vendrato CRM systems</a></article>
<article><h3>Automations</h3><p class="st-price">Priced to scope</p><p>Workflow mapping, integrations and testing, so a new enquiry triggers the next step on its own. My part: GoHighLevel workflows and Make or n8n scenarios that move data between your form, CRM and inbox.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://vendrato.com/automations">Vendrato automations</a></article>
<article><h3>Care after launch</h3><p class="st-price">From US$100 a month</p><p>Four hours of support each month for minor revisions, security patches and routine upkeep. Larger changes are scoped separately.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://vendrato.com/websites">Vendrato maintenance</a></article>
</div>
<p class="st-also">The same team also builds <a class="st-inline" href="https://vendrato.com/voice-ai">voice AI</a> and <a class="st-inline" href="https://vendrato.com/app-development">custom apps</a>, so a website can grow into a connected system without changing studios.</p>
<dl class="st-facts"><div><dt>First</dt><dd>A free 30-minute call about your business and current setup</dd></div><div><dt>Then</dt><dd>A written scope, timeline and fixed price, with weekly demos</dd></div><div><dt>At launch</dt><dd>Your code, accounts and documentation, in your name</dd></div></dl>
</div></section>
<ContactBand/>
</Site>
